30,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems joint ventures here often fail due to rota disputes. Also, home visits have a high failure rate due to access issues.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Interestingly, a previous call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for the elderly, but the booking system fails to track any work without a fixed slot.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have a serious nursing shortage and high agency costs, but the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is tighter than we thought, and notably, off-site contacts bring in no regional funding, whereas on-site sessions do.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Our parking and rooms are already at capacity. Furthermore, getting data agreements with outside surgeries is a nightmare that takes over a year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site work earns nothing, we must be cautious about home-based programs.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, if midwifery has slack, perhaps a program utilizing them would be sustainable.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"That is a fair point, Jonathan. The ward nurses are far too stretched for anything new.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, if the building is full, we can't afford any program that requires new floor space given the budget cuts.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,Exactly. Anything requiring new rooms or complex external data links seems impractical right now.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the readmission data you found is promising. Is there a way to do that without risking the ""invisible"" work problem?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It would need to be structured. If we use the existing slack Misaki mentioned, we might find a balance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We should avoid adding pressure to the ward staff or the therapists who are already leaving.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Logically, an on-site program using existing staff slack and generating tariffs is the only viable path.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. We must avoid the parking lot and the data agreement hurdles.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we are leaning toward something internal and staff-supported.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have enough information to evaluate the candidates once they are presented.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I concur.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,Let us see the options.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am ready.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
