55,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at these, the Home Follow-Up Team (A) risks the access issues and funding gaps I found. Chronic Care (C) seems too dependent on those slow data agreements.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Day Rehabilitation Unit (B) would help patients, but Misaki mentioned the therapy staff are leaving for the city. That's a risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Yes, B is risky. However, the Perinatal Support Service (D) uses midwifery, where I found there is actually slack in the rota.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shion,,"D is on-site, meaning it generates tariffs and avoids the budget drain of off-site travel. It's the most fiscally sound.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"D uses existing departments. As long as it doesn't require new construction, it fits our capacity better than a new Rehab Unit.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree. D avoids the ""joint venture"" trap if the midwifery and pediatric departments are aligned, and it's on-site.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"A is tempting because of the readmission figures, but the booking system and funding issues make it a ghost program.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Misaki,,D is the only one that doesn't put more pressure on the exhausted ward nurses.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shion,,"The logic is clear. D is the only option that aligns with the budget, the tariffs, and the staffing reality.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shizue,,I support D. It is the most absorbable option for the hospital.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm satisfied with D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I am as well.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shion,,D is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
